# tiberius: the engine's local patches, against upstream d6708a4aae15b4860000d54c8af9e84d684bce09.
#
# The first two changes are one patch because they interleave in the same regions: the
# host expert tier and the DAX window both edit expert_source.{hpp,cpp} (the
# `pin_cache_complement` guard, and the `pinned()`/`device_alias()` path) and the
# same resident-tier block in generate.cpp, so they cannot be applied separately
# in either order without conflicting.
#
# 1. The host expert tier, the reason the service passes --resident-cpu-mib: a
#    rank-ordered, size-capped DRAM complement of the VRAM expert cache, plus the
#    relaxed --resident-cpu-experts requirement that let it coexist with the
#    adaptive cache (it no longer demands --adapt-every 0).
#
# 2. STRATA_REGISTER_DAX, the sliding DAX window: cudaHostRegister cannot pin the
#    46.84 GiB pack at once - the driver caps TOTAL registered host memory at 6144
#    MiB on this box, measured and independent of free RAM - so the engine
#    registers a window of whole, page-aligned layers, follows the layer-ordered
#    prefill walk, and rotates the window (draining the copy stream first) once
#    per budget.  Every layer the window holds is DMA-able by the device, so the
#    prompt path stops staging those experts through the copy threads.  It needs
#    the fsdax_longterm_pin=1 kernel opt-in (pkgs/kernel-patches/fsdax-longterm-pin.patch);
#    without it cudaHostRegister is refused, the engine reports it once and keeps
#    the pageable path.  Measured on the real corpus: prefill 13,136 -> 10,223 ms
#    for a 4292-token prompt (327 -> 420 tok/s), decode unchanged.
#
# 3. STRATA_DENSE_FP16, the dense GEMMs on the FP16 tensor cores.  Turing has FP16
#    tensor cores and no BF16 ones, so the dense GEMMs (Gemm::bf16 in
#    src/prefill/gemm.cu, 482 calls per 4292-token prompt) were served by cuBLAS'
#    FP32 SIMT fallback (`magma_sgemmEx_kernel`, 155 calls / 335.7 ms of a 9.2 s
#    prompt).  The flag converts each operand pair to FP16 in the existing 64 MiB
#    dequantization scratch and calls the same tensor-core path the FP16
#    projections already use (accumulation stays FP32).  bf16 -> fp16 is exact
#    for every value in fp16's finite range (8 vs 10 mantissa bits), and the
#    operands were measured well inside it (max|X| 103.5, max|W| 11.56 against
#    fp16's 65504; STRATA_GEMM_DEBUG prints them).  Measured 2026-10-01 on the
#    real corpus, 3 runs/arm, flag on vs off in the same binary: 4292-token
#    prompt 10,350 -> 9,845 ms (-4.9% mean, -5.8% median), 3514-token 9,782 ->
#    9,179 (-6.2%); total kernel time 1564 -> 1302 ms (-16.8%).  The prompt-path
#    state hash changes (different accumulation order; relative max deviation
#    1.6e-6..5.3e-5) - it is a numerics change, hence opt-in, not a default.
#
# Merged by hand 2026-10-01 from the former pkgs/strata-sm75/hosttier.patch
# (applied to d6708a4) and the tiberius-dma worktree's window change (whose base
# was d6708a4 + that same host tier).  The worktree's unrelated stager
# instrumentation and self-issuing-streamer commits are deliberately NOT part of
# this patch.
